Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:34:49 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0803): no-display state in All-displays mode

AC-52, DEF-5 (whole-product review finding 14). When the host's display
list became empty while the client viewed All displays, sync_peer_info
went to updateCurDisplay, which returns early without a display
rectangle, so the last frame stayed up with no explanation. Upstream's
"No Displays" message existed only for a single selected display.

The empty list is now decided first, in every view mode
(remotesmith/display_topology.dart): the client releases held keys,
held mouse buttons and local input capture, and shows "No display
available". The message can be closed without ending the session, so
the view resumes if a display comes back.

Test: flutter/test/remotesmith_display_topology_test.dart.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
